            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the hospital course of your patient, a 20-year-old male, admitted on 23/05/2023 with classic signs of acute appendicitis, including right lower quadrant pain, fever, and elevated inflammatory markers. Clinical examination and abdominal ultrasound confirmed the diagnosis. The patient was adequately prepared and underwent a laparoscopic emergency appendectomy on 24/05/2023 without intraoperative complications. Postoperatively, he received intravenous antibiotics and analgesics, with prompt clinical improvement. Wound healing was satisfactory, vital signs remained stable throughout, and the patient was mobilized early. He was discharged home on 28/05/2023 in good general condition. Please ensure follow-up in approximately two weeks for wound inspection and review of the histopathological findings of the appendix specimen. Should any concerns arise, please do not hesitate to contact our surgical department.</div>"
            },
